> The source is just a repost of Cookies by Jesse Szewczyk. 

Melt @butter{2%sticks}(unsalted) in a #small saucepan{} over medium heat. Continue cooking, stirring often to prevent burning, until the butter foams and then darkens in color slightly and is very fragrant, about ~{4%minutes}. 

Transfer the butter immediately to a heatproof bowl, and let it cool at room temperature for ~{20%minutes}.

Heat the oven to 350ºF. 

Line two #sheet pan{} with parchment paper. 

Combine @flour{2.5%cups}, @cream of tartar{2%tsp}, @baking soda{1%tsp}, @salt{1/2%tsp} in a large bowl.

With a paddle attachment on a #stand mixer{}, combine the cooled butter, @sugar{1%cup}, and @brown sugar{1/2%cup}. Beat at medium speed until combined, about ~{1%minute}.

Turn the mixer off and add @eggs{2}(beaten, room temperature), @vanilla extract{1%tsp}, and @?bourbon{2%tbsp}(whiskey, dark spiced rum, etc. all work). Mix on medium speed until pale yellow and ribbony, about ~{2-3%minutes}.

With the mixer running on low speed, gradually add the flour mixture until just combined.

In a small bowl, combine @sugar{1/2%cup} and @cinnamon{1%tbsp}.

Portion out dough into 2 tbsp balls.

Roll in the cinnamon sugar mixture and place the dough balls at least 3 inches apart on the prepared baking sheets.

Bake both sheets at the same time for about ~{8-11%minutes}, until the tops of the cookies are lightly browned. Swap the top and bottom sheets midway through baking.

Let cool slightly on the baking sheets, then transfer to a wire rack to cool.